  "source_ref": "ALINX Z7-P User Manual section 3.9 FMC Connector pin-assignment table (pp.57-68), extracted from PDF text coordinates; FMC connector positions fully verified against the official Z7-P base-board schematic Rev 1.0 (sheets 15-17, FMC HPC J-symbol; net-to-VITA-position join, 163/164 positions exact, one C26/LA27_P label-offset artifact resolved visually). Balls are on the ACU7EVC SoM's ZU7EV (carrier FMC signals route through the SoM connectors). EXCLUDED as not documented to reach the FPGA: the carrier PCB wires HA00-HA22 (23 pairs) from the FMC connector to the SoM socket (schematic Connector_1/2 sheets); FMC JTAG exists only on the FMC sheet and never reaches the socket, but the kit-level UG pin table omits them and no SoM-side doc maps them to ZU7EV balls - the UG intro's '59 pairs to BANK28/64/65' counts these HA pairs, so they may be live with other SoMs; treated as not-routed for this kit. VREF_A_M2C (H1) wired but excluded by repo convention. CLK2/CLK3_BIDIR, HB bus and DP8/9 positions are no-connect. GBTCLK/CLK paths are direct-wired (no clock mux sheets in the 19-page schematic); population of clock routes visually unremarkable but not BOM-verified. CORRECTION (schematic-verified during the Z11-P join): the UG row FMC_PG_C2M -> K9 is an erratum - schematic sheet 15 shows FMC pin D1 (PG_C2M) dead-ending at a 4.7k pullup to +3.3V, while ball K9 (B87_L8_P, socket J29:63) carries TRIG_IN from the external trigger connector (sheet 18); PG_C2M removed.",
